A||||31||Oreif||Fiero Store Responds!!||||14||
Z||000000||Oreif||09-29-2001||01:58 PM||||Just received this Email:<P>To Rodney Dickman and The Fiero Community:<BR> <BR>The Fiero Store would like to extend its sincerest apologies to Rodney<BR>Dickman for producing an unauthorized copy of his select arm rebuild kits.<BR>After receiving a number of calls from our customers asking us to offer some<BR>of Rodney's parts, we immediately contacted Mr. Dickman. We were hoping to<BR>use a supplier from within the Fiero community with a good reputation for<BR>quality parts. Unfortunately, Mr. Dickman made it quite clear, in no<BR>uncertain terms, that he did not want to do business with The Fiero Store.<BR>As a result, we were forced to manufacture the select arm rebuild kits<BR>ourselves in order to bring our customers the part they demanded.<BR>Regretfully, we were irresponsible in designing a part that was identical to<BR>Mr. Dickman's select arm rebuild kit. There was never any malice intended<BR>toward Mr. Dickman or his business. We have and will continue to recommend<BR>RodneyDickman.com to all of our customers who need parts that we do not<BR>offer. As a gesture of good faith, we will also send Mr. Dickman our entire<BR>inventory of select arm rebuild kits. The Fiero Store will no longer carry<BR>this part and will direct all of our customers looking for that part to Mr.<BR>Dickman.<BR> <BR>We would also like to sincerely apologize to our customers and to the Fiero<BR>community at large for inadvertently abusing their trust. Our only intention<BR>in carrying the select arm rebuild kits was to give our customers the part<BR>they asked for. Had we viewed Rodney Dickman as a "competitor," rather than<BR>an ally, we certainly would not have asked him to supply us with parts nor<BR>would we recommend him to so many of our customers. We have a lot of respect<BR>for Rodney and all of the hard work he has done to help Fiero owners.<BR> <BR>In the coming months and years, you will see many new products coming from<BR>The Fiero Store. Many of our new parts will not be found anywhere else in<BR>the world. Some of those new products may be similar to parts offered by<BR>Rodney Dickman. In order for a company to grow, it must provide its<BR>customers with the products and service that they demand, regardless of who<BR>else may offer a similar product or service. However, the Fiero community<BR>can rest assured that none of our new products will be exactly the same as<BR>Rodney's. We will take great care in making sure that our products offer<BR>unique value separate and apart from anything offered by Mr. Dickman.<BR> <BR>We hope that Mr. Dickman and the rest of the Fiero community will accept our<BR>apology. We made a mistake, have taken steps to correct that mistake, and<BR>will take full responsibility for our actions. We look forward to continuing<BR>to serve Fiero owners around the world to the best of our ability and we<BR>thank all of our customers for their continued support.<BR> <BR>Sincerely,<BR>Smitty<BR>President<BR>The Fiero Store<BR><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">       <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Mach10||09-29-2001||02:06 PM||||Professionalism reigns! That's a good gesture...||||reg||14
Z||000002||85 gt fiero||09-29-2001||02:06 PM||||i think that was the best thing for the "fiero store" to do, was to stop selling them.   Randy||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||09-29-2001||02:15 PM||||Wow! <P>The customers (and the Fiero community) have spoken. And were heard.<P>Very cool. And a very professional response.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000004||KissMySSFiero||09-29-2001||02:17 PM||||that good to see and hear.  i know they did appologize, but do you think anything they offer now was a copy of someone's design even from a few years back.  just a thought.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <BR>88FORMULA<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>        <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||09-29-2001||02:18 PM||||BTW...<P>I just received the same e-mail. <BR>Well done, all.<P>Steve||||reg||1
Z||000006||skitime||09-29-2001||02:39 PM||||I feel the Fiero Store should be back in our good graces.  Now only have they righted their wrong but they also sent Rodney their remaining inventories of the select arm rebuild kits. I am impressed with their actions.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Doni Hagan||09-29-2001||04:11 PM||||That was a very classy way of resolving a sticky issue. Congradulations to the Fiero Store. That wasn't capitulation, that was cooperation.  ||||reg||6
Z||000008||pontiacs4me||09-29-2001||04:30 PM||||I bet the fierostore sh!t their pants when they found out what was happening here.  they made a wise decision to do what they did, and I bet it wont ever happen again.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||09-29-2001||04:40 PM||||Too bad Rodney isn't the only one to be blind sided by them. Just found out they use to have Nolan Concepts supply the cold air intake, They canceled the orders from him then made a copy and sold it as their own!!<P>Wonder who else has been copied?||||reg||8
Z||000010||Dslice||09-29-2001||05:41 PM||||I've bought from both Rodney and the Fiero Store and always been very pleased by both. There apology is good with me I would hate to see a source of parts and supplies. In the case of directly copying Rodney's product was wrong. If they developed there own from scratch that would have been fine, that's the way capitalism works. I feel the cold air intake thing is all fair. The cold air intake is no complex thing to make or produce and they're all pretty much the same. I could easily create and produce my own with no problem and would that be copy a product, I don't think so. If some one exactly copied there engine dress up things  exactly than would be wrong. Good Ideas get copied, and as long as there not exactly the same then that's ok. I think Rodney did the right thing in going to the Fiero Community to resolve the problem, and I'm very glad that the Fiero Store is trying to make amends because I have enjoyed doing business with both groups and hope to do so in the future.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Bazooka||09-29-2001||05:44 PM||||*****************************<BR>This really makes me wonder what kind of business they are running at TFS. If this type of infringement was done with Rodneys' design, what else is in their catalog that has been copied or stolen? This does not sound like a random mistake. <BR>****************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Too bad Rodney isn't the only one to be blind sided by them. Just found out they use to have Nolan Concepts supply the cold air intake, They canceled the orders from him then made a copy and sold it as their own!!<P>Wonder who else has been copied?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||dennis_6||09-29-2001||06:39 PM||||I sent an email to complain to the Fiero store and also got the same response.  I belive the Fiero store did the right thing.  Amazingly the Fiero community was heard!!<P>------------------<BR> Friends don't let friends drive rice.||||reg||6
Z||000013||Rodney||09-29-2001||07:24 PM||||When I confronted the Fiero Store about copying a unique design they basically said too bad. We will do whatever we want and we will not hesitate to copy more of your product line. They only changed their tune once many Fiero owners told them what they did was wrong. What concerns me is that they had to be pressured into doing the right thing. I compare this to the recent terrorist activities. The Taliban was very hard lined until they seen the rest of the world unit against them. I am a one man business. I am reaching the limits of the amount of products I am able to offer and wish to remain at that level. I see the Fiero Store as trying to do away with me instead of letting me supply odd and non existent products. We could have easily worked together thru the years but they have taken a stance that is not beneficial to anyone including themselves I feel. It is too bad they choose this path. I used to send business their way daily. I can not do that anymore. We all lose from this. I have a list of maybe 100 or more new product ideas - most of which I will never have the time to develope. To bad the Fiero Store can't come up with some new stuff instead of copying other peoples products. There is much to be done in the years to come for parts for the Fieros.  <P>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Fiero5||09-29-2001||08:21 PM||||I had forwarded my responces from both the Forum here and ones I had sent to the Fiero lists also. I love how quickly they reacted to our feelings about this. I think they discovered how quickly there world was crashing down around them for screwing one of our own.<P>I would just like to say that at least the outcome was the best scenario of what we all wanted. We spoke as a groupe and we were heard loud and clear!<P>I agree with Rodney that it is sad that they only decided to do what they did, only after we all complained. They should not have done what they did to begin with. It was only after they got caught with their pants down, that they decided to do this.<P>Hopefully this was the wake up call that they needed to not even think of trying this again with anybody.<P>Congrats Rodney.<P>Steve Kelley<P>------------------<BR>                                <IMG SRC="http://a1040.g.akamai.net/f/1040/759/1h/206.29.192.139/info/pics/sept11.jpg">                             <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||7
Z||000015||stimpy||09-29-2001||08:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rodney:<BR><B> What concerns me is that they had to be pressured into doing the right thing. I compare this to the recent terrorist activities. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OH MY GOD! YOU DID NOT JUST SAY THAT! I cannot believe that you would have the nerve to compare the "horror" of possibly loosing a couple of sales of some little widget to the very real pain and suffering of the entire nation from the loss of thousands of REAL PEOPLE! <BR>Don't get me wrong, Rodney. I think any guy making a quarter out of fifteen cents to support the Fiero community <B>deserves</B> the suport in kind when the big guys steal his lunch money. I commend everyone for supporting you, as I commend The Fiero Store for making good (although obviously not good enough for your liking). However this Christ complex that you are dishing out comparing The Fiero Store to blood thirsty mass murderers just leaves me feeling dirty all over. <P>Think twice before you click submit.||||reg||1
Z||000016||8Ball||09-29-2001||09:00 PM||||I think Rodney is comnpletely in the right in EVERYTHING he said. Maybe you should read the post again.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Cheever3000||09-29-2001||09:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>...we were forced to manufacture the select arm rebuild kits ourselves in order to bring our customers the part they demanded.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Forced?  Bad choice of words I'm sure.  One could think forced by greed, but the context seems to be forced by the natural desire to satisfy the customers, and that doesn't necessarily mean greed.  I'll accept their apology, but I agree with the above posts who wonder how many others they have copied from.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||stimpy||09-29-2001||09:23 PM||||Umm, did a pretty good job reading the first time, but just for the benefit of your doubt, 8ball, I read it again. I stand by what I say. Perhaps you should reread my commnts. I don't feel it is right to come along and steal one's intellectual property, but I don't feel that is tantamount to the worst terrorist atrocity in the history of our nation. Moreover, The Fiero Store has reversed their position and has made moves to remedy this whole situation. I don't thing what they did in any way deserves comparison to a "terrorist attack".<BR>Sorry, I just don't buy that kind of hype.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Mach10||09-29-2001||09:30 PM||||Stimpy: Agreed. What FS did was shitty, but not THAT shitty. Whatever. The problem seems resolved...||||reg||13
Z||000020||West Coast Fiero||09-29-2001||10:13 PM||||unfortunately they are always going to be there, and they will always be "borrowing" design ideas - part that sucks is that is just buisness<P>I'm curious though, does the FS sponser any shows or events, give a hand in participation to key events in the Fiero community - or are they just there to make the buck?<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000021||FieroRyan||09-29-2001||10:59 PM||||Stimpy, I believe that Rodney meant they were like the Taliban, not the actual attackers.  <P>"The Taliban was very hard lined until they seen the rest of the world unite against them."<P>Personally, I think this comparison works, as it isn't saying anything about the terrorists, just that the Taliban (fiero store) only did what they wanted until the world (fiero community) united against them.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||FieroKyle||09-30-2001||12:30 AM||||LoL, once again Stimpy picks apart somebody's comment that really wasn't "that" innaporiate to start another agruement Mr. lawyer, lol. Just messing with ya Stimpster.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||JSocha||09-30-2001||02:16 AM||||In the world of manufacturing, "It is a dog eat dog world".<P>Our product has been replicated by our competitors as well as start up companies.<P>We have patents on some of our products, but all they have to do is change a few minor thing and its classified as different and gets buy the laws.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>But, then again, our company (as well as many others) does the same.  <P>We see how we can replicate a product based on the market it is getting, make it better then the original and see if we can make it cheaper at the same time based to hopefully gain the business based on the demand in the market place.<P>Just looking at this from a manufacturing perspective.  <P>I personally don't support either side here and would do business with either RD or FS based on who has the better product at the best price.<P>Sorry if that that may offend anyone.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||Sage||09-30-2001||08:44 AM||||Glad to hear they did the right thing.<P>They made a mistake and rectified it in what I would consider a very classy manor.<P>  Maybe we don't have the entire history.  If a large concern came to me and said "We would like to buy your product and resell it.", I think I would probably consider that steady production sales.  I don't have to mess with anything or anyone, but making my product, which suits me.  If they said, "If you don't sell us your product, we are going to copy it ourselves and sell that.", I would consider that grounds for legal action.  I have had very good experiences with Rodney in the past, he is a very important part of the Fiero community, in my opinion.  Haven't had much dealings with the FS but they send me their catologs, and they seem to have some hard to get stuff.  At last check don't try to order a 2.5 cyl. head though, that is listed in their catolog, as they tell you they are not available!  <P>Sorry to get long winded, but I just wanted to express that I think they(FS)handled this in the best way they could have under the given circumstances.  Rodney, why not work together, with them and let them do the advertising, shipping, handling, promo, etc.  maybe they could even help fund some of your r&d!  Don't mean to get wacko on you, I just usually try to find a way for people to work together and/or get along than being at each other's throat.  After all, I DON'T think we are talking about the mentality behind the recent sick attack on our nation and on freedom and our way of life in general.  <P>If you want to stay a one man operation and take care of everything yourself, I can understand that too.  You will just have to be prepared to be immitated when you come up with something that works well.  We do have more than one version of the automobile you know!  Viva Fiero!<P>Sorry if anyone is offended by anything said here, it is only the thoughts of a "crazy man"  LOL <P>Have a good one!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 09-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||firstfiero||09-30-2001||11:00 AM||||          Well I've stayed kinda silent during this but here's my 2 cents. The fiero store did what corporations do all the  time. hell at least they asked him to be their supplier befor making their own. I'm sure that's more then alot of inventors get. Not to say that it was right what they did. It's unfortunatly it's just a fact of life in the business world. The only reason your letters worked in this instance is because of the numbers. Were all small close knit community. The fiero store realised that they need us. Theirs a saying "don't ****  where you eat." And when the group that your targeting is as small as us it is never more true.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000026||Dave Gunsul||09-30-2001||01:08 PM||||Well as always it seems I am on the more unpopular side of this.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>I have to agree with JSocha and First Fiero,<BR>this thing happens all the time with business, no it doesn't make it right but it<BR>does happen all the time. If I remember correctly they did offer to buy them from you and you refused and not with just one thing but two. (coolant tubes and select arm<BR>kits) Then you go on to say that you and they could've worked together in the future,<BR>that just doesn't add up. I like your products Rodney and I think you contribute to the Fiero community with your unique parts and knowledge. I have also sent people to you so don't think i'm coming down on you<BR>for no reason but what really made me say something is that you compared a few sales to human beings being killed! I don't really think you meant it that way, or at least I hope not, but that was a very poor choice of words to describe the situation.<P>BTW the Fiero store has donated door prizes<BR>to NIFE's Fierorama so I don't think that they're just in it for the buck.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000027||Stage-2GT||09-30-2001||02:02 PM||||  Now here's an idea!! Did not Rodney copy his items from someone else's products. I mean, his intent was to supply the Fiero community with parts that were no longer available right? That means the those same parts did exist. I have no way of knowing, but did Mr. Dickman get the OEM's permission to remanufacture these parts? Like I said I have no way of knowing, for sure. <BR> I have bought things from Rodney and was glad he had them available, I have also bought things from the Fiero Store and was glad that they too had them available. Now it seems to me, that you can walk into any parts house and find the same products offered by several different vendors. How come no one is up in arms about that? So what if the Fiero Store also offered the select arm rebuild kits? So what if the were identical to Rodney's? Does this mean that Mobil One should bow out to STP or Fram for making the same products? <BR>  Here we are again with the Archie-vs-FieroShop mentality. Stimpy was right and you all should re-read his first post. This topic has gone in a totally stupid direction and defies all logic!<P>S2GT <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>"If Hate Was Money, I Would Own The World"||||reg||3
Z||000028||Oreif||09-30-2001||03:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Stage-2GT:<BR><B>  Now here's an idea!! Did not Rodney copy his items from someone else's products. I mean, his intent was to supply the Fiero community with parts that were no longer available right? That means the those same parts did exist. I have no way of knowing, but did Mr. Dickman get the OEM's permission to remanufacture these parts? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think you mis-understood something. The OEM parts are no longer available and over time the nylon bushings wear out. Rodney re-designed the assembly using brass bushings. There is no problem selling "similar" products but to come out and publicly announce you copied someone else's parts and sell them for less is wrong. Then in their original Email they stated that if anything else he made was deemed popular they would copy them too. As your example of Mobil 1 vs. STP, they have differences. STP didn't come out and say "we copied you", They put out a similar product.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Rodney||09-30-2001||06:09 PM||||Quote:<P>After receiving a number of calls from our customers asking us to offer some<BR>of Rodney's parts, we immediately contacted Mr. Dickman. We were hoping to<BR>use a supplier from within the Fiero community with a good reputation for<BR>quality parts. Unfortunately, Mr. Dickman made it quite clear, in no<BR>uncertain terms, that he did not want to do business with The Fiero Store.<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>The Fiero Store offers nobody a dealer discount. Nobody. Even those such as Ed Parks. But they use that excuse for me? I get calls all the time from Fiero owners looking for parts. If I do not sell it I send them on to whomever sells it if anyone does. That does not force me to copy other peoples parts so I can sell them. The Fiero Store is welcome to buy all the parts they want from me at list price. I never said I would not sell to them. I will not wholesale to them. I am not a supplier to the Fiero Store. If someone calls apparently they are too lame to send them to me. Sorry. This is just plain envy and they wanted to cash in on some of my parts since they have a good reputation of working and are good quality. Instead of coming up with new products nobody else offers like I do they have to copy others. I expect them to copy more of the parts I have developed in the near future. They openly admit it. They seem to want to be the sole Fiero parts supplier in the world and appear to be looking to over run all who stand in their way. They are in this situation as the parts they have found from GM (most appariently they have been able to buy at pennies on the dollar - GM old stock destined for the dumster) are running out and they have to develope new sources to keep up their profits. <P><BR>Thanks,<BR>Rodney Dickman<BR>New web page! <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000030||Fiero5||09-30-2001||10:05 PM||||Rodney: You now have an apology from the Fiero Store and the fact that they are going to send you all of the stock of these copied items, etc. We as a Fiero community also have their apology. they said they were wrong in doing this and have stated in specifics what they are going to do to make it right.<P>I hope in the face of these new statements from the Fiero Store, you will at least hold off for now on continuing to bash them and mention what you expect they may do in copying more parts in the near future.<BR>They admitted they were wrong and have apologized to us and to you specifically. Yes they shouldn't have done what they did in the first place, but the best they can do now is what they are doing. <P>I think that if the Fiero Store ever tries this type of crap again, they will be in an even worse position than what we were all mentioning we were planning and willing to do just a few days ago.<BR>You know the old saying: Fool me once, shame on you. Fool me twice, shame on me.<BR>Or the crying wolf example. They said they will now do X, Y and Z to make it right, and we need to give them the time and space to do it. We, the Fiero community, are giving them that room to make good  as they have now stepped forward and stated they are going to do. If they however do not follow up and actually do what they say, and/or do this again to anyone down the road, I am pretty confident that this Fiero communiuty will take it as an even worst insult against all of us.<P>You have heard it many, many times how much we appreciate you Rodney as a fellow Fiero person and as a Fiero parts supplier. I think what you have seen in the last few days, has backed that up a hundred fold. I think we can all agree that a lot of us in the Fiero community stepped up to the plate this weekend and helped out one of our own. I think the response we all got was more than we could have expected, and the best we could have ever wished for. However, we all need to let the seeds we planted now do it's work. Let's all cool down now and let the Fiero Store do the only things they can do now to make what they did as right as possible under the circumstances.<P>One thing is for sure, all of us that are aware of this (and that is a lot of people between the e-mail lists and Pennocks) will never look at the Fiero Store the same way again. No matter how many times they apologize and no matter how clean they keep their nose from this day forward, this has and will for a long time hurt them in many areas even beyond  financially. Some in ways that they may not realize for weeks or months to come.<P>This weekend the Fiero community spoke. This weekend our voice was also heard loud and clear!<P>Steve<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero5 (edited 09-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000031||firstfiero||09-30-2001||10:45 PM||||    Sorry guys the more I think about it the more I feel the fiero store did nothing wrong. They offered to buy them from him and he wasn't interested. He was dumb enough not to patten his new design so it's just smart business for a place like the fiero store who try to stock everything fiero related to reproduce them . I now must say I don't think the fiero store owed anyone an apology and I for one would still buy stuff from them with or without it. <P>------------------<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by firstfiero (edited 10-01-2001).]||||reg||9
